/**
 * @page topic_packet_queue Packet Queues
 * @ingroup network
 *
 * Queues own their nodes and payload references. Use packet_queue_push_copy()
 * for a borrowed view, packet_queue_push_take() to move a buffer without copying,
 * or packet_queue_push_shared() for immutable fan-out. Successful take clears
 * the caller pointer; rejection preserves it. All operations return contextual
 * asciichat_error_t errors.
 *
 * Every queue has both a packet-count limit and a byte limit. The default
 * overflow policy rejects new packets. DROP_OLDEST must be explicitly selected
 * for independently discardable media such as raw frames or audio blocks. Do
 * not select it for dependency-bearing encoded video without recovery logic.
 *
 * One queue mutex protects admission, list mutation, accounting and reclamation.
 * Nodes use the shared buffer API; there is no independent node allocator.
 * Dequeue transfers the existing node without another allocation. Release with
 * packet_queue_free_packet(). Dequeued packets can outlive their queue.
 *
 * Stop rejects new admissions and hides queued data from consumers. Clear and
 * destroy still drain stopped queues. Join queue users before destruction.
 * Queued storage is released automatically; already dequeued packets remain
 * owned by their consumers.
 */
